        <mxCell id="kg_note" parent="kaggle" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#0A2530;strokeColor=#20BEFF;dashed=1;fontColor=#CFEFFF;fontSize=9;arcSize=12;spacing=6" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why off-machine:&lt;/b&gt; local 4GB box has no torch; Kaggle has no Ollama/MCP, so it cannot host the live pipeline. P100 is sm_60 and this torch needs sm_70+, so the trainer falls back to CPU (~0.27s over 188 rows) — the GPU was never load-bearing. Kaggle exists here to &lt;i&gt;execute and cross-check&lt;/i&gt; the torch backend.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
